1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:44,087 --> 00:01:45,587
I've had enough of you!

17
00:01:47,507 --> 00:01:49,677
I'll take anything you can spare...

18
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:56,477
Thank you very much.

19
00:01:56,477 --> 00:02:01,477
Wolf and the Grand Scheme

20
00:02:17,787 --> 00:02:19,537
You're back early.

21
00:02:45,687 --> 00:02:46,977
Holo.

22
00:02:47,817 --> 00:02:48,847
I'm sorry.

23
00:02:58,037 --> 00:03:00,917
Here are three Lumione I managed to collect by myself.

24
00:03:01,737 --> 00:03:06,297
The remaining forty-four Lumione are beyond my grasp.

25
00:03:06,877 --> 00:03:11,287
The only thing I can think of is to go to a gambling parlor with the money,

26
00:03:11,717 --> 00:03:15,297
but you'd probably have more luck with that than I would.

27
00:03:16,007 --> 00:03:19,427
If I'm going to fail, I'd rather put the money to good use.

28
00:03:19,427 --> 00:03:23,957
Owing three more Lumione won't make much of a difference anyway.

29
00:04:04,207 --> 00:04:05,367
You fool!

30
00:04:06,147 --> 00:04:08,007
Hurry up and come back!

31
00:04:10,897 --> 00:04:12,567
What's going on?

32
00:04:15,427 --> 00:04:17,737
Oh, I'm terribly sorry!

33
00:04:17,737 --> 00:04:20,197
I just dropped this from the window.

34
00:04:20,197 --> 00:04:22,567
You've got to be kidding me.

35
00:04:24,537 --> 00:04:25,787
You fool.

36
00:04:27,077 --> 00:04:28,417
Sorry.

37
00:04:28,417 --> 00:04:29,907
What do you mean by that?

38
00:04:30,417 --> 00:04:31,917
What are you sorry for?

39
00:04:33,467 --> 00:04:36,807
What would you have done if I took the money and fled?

40
00:04:39,007 --> 00:04:40,837
I wouldn't have minded.

41
00:04:41,257 --> 00:04:45,387
Because I failed, I won't be able to fulfill our contract.

42
00:04:46,307 --> 00:04:47,987
That money would cover your travel expenses.

43
00:04:48,767 --> 00:04:53,597
You... You're going to give <i>me</i> money... so I can keep traveling?

44
00:04:56,237 --> 00:04:57,987
Y-Yeah...

45
00:04:57,987 --> 00:04:59,947
I'm the one at fault, you know!

46
00:04:59,947 --> 00:05:02,367
You would have been able to borrow money if not for me!

47
00:05:02,367 --> 00:05:04,907
Why aren't you angry at me?

48
00:05:04,907 --> 00:05:06,977
How come you're not blaming me for anything?

49
00:05:08,787 --> 00:05:11,547
You followed me because you were worried about me.

50
00:05:11,547 --> 00:05:13,497
I can't be angry at you for—

51
00:05:13,507 --> 00:05:14,957
You fool!

52
00:05:17,377 --> 00:05:18,507
You...

53
00:05:20,547 --> 00:05:21,087
Watch out!

54
00:05:31,137 --> 00:05:33,477
You're a sucker after all!

55
00:05:33,477 --> 00:05:34,937
A... sucker?

56
00:05:34,937 --> 00:05:36,607
I'm right, aren't I?

57
00:05:36,607 --> 00:05:39,407
I followed you out of my selfishness.

58
00:05:39,407 --> 00:05:43,047
You had every right to be mad at me.

59
00:05:43,047 --> 00:05:45,907
But then you <i>apologize</i> just because you slapped my hands away!

60
00:05:45,907 --> 00:05:48,287
You even came back to say sorry!

61
00:05:49,167 --> 00:05:50,897
Because I <i>was</i> sorry.

62
00:05:51,627 --> 00:05:56,527
I felt like I did something that couldn't be forgiven no matter how many times I apologized.

63
00:05:57,217 --> 00:06:00,047
That's why I wanted to do all I could,

64
00:06:00,717 --> 00:06:05,047
but it seems that only hurt you more. I'm sorry.

65
00:06:06,057 --> 00:06:07,307
Would you...

66
00:06:08,597 --> 00:06:10,597
Answer me this one question.

67
00:06:11,937 --> 00:06:14,807
You're so kind.

68
00:06:15,897 --> 00:06:18,317
W-Why is that?

69
00:06:20,857 --> 00:06:23,407
My personality, I suppose.

70
00:06:23,407 --> 00:06:25,487
Y-You fool!

71
00:06:25,487 --> 00:06:28,827
Personality? Personality, you say?

72
00:06:28,827 --> 00:06:32,197
As a male, you have to say that it's because you're in love with me, even if you don't mean it!

73
00:06:32,197 --> 00:06:33,417
You fool!

74
00:06:33,417 --> 00:06:35,497
S-Sorry.

75
00:06:35,497 --> 00:06:37,327
To tell you the truth, I...

76
00:06:37,327 --> 00:06:42,257
There are times when I want to hear sweet words even if they're a lie,

77
00:06:42,257 --> 00:06:46,347
but once it's too late, hearing those words makes you want to slap the speaker's face.

78
00:06:46,347 --> 00:06:47,967
Which situation do you think you're in?

79
00:06:48,977 --> 00:06:50,887
T-The latter.

80
00:06:52,857 --> 00:06:54,767
This is unbelievable.

81
00:06:54,767 --> 00:06:57,317
I can't believe you're so softhearted!

82
00:06:57,317 --> 00:07:01,987
You probably thought you'd be taking advantage of me if you said something like that, but...

83
00:07:03,197 --> 00:07:04,477
It's pathetic, I know.

84
00:07:04,987 --> 00:07:08,537
I still do want to hear you say it.

85
00:07:08,537 --> 00:07:09,857
Let's do it over.

86
00:07:16,627 --> 00:07:20,627
Why are you so kind?

87
00:07:21,127 --> 00:07:23,337
Because you're special to me.

88
00:07:45,867 --> 00:07:49,077
For goodness sake. What are we even doing?

89
00:07:49,077 --> 00:07:51,197
Y-You're the one who made me do it!

90
00:07:53,247 --> 00:07:56,287
Well, it served as good practice for you, didn't it?

91
00:07:59,337 --> 00:08:01,127
Still, I must say.

92
00:08:02,167 --> 00:08:04,797
Next time, just make me angry. Okay?

93
00:08:04,797 --> 00:08:07,757
I appreciate the fact that you're a considerate person,

94
00:08:07,757 --> 00:08:13,047
but there are things that can be settled quicker by screaming at each other.

95
00:08:16,937 --> 00:08:18,107
As you wish.

96
00:08:20,277 --> 00:08:21,737
So...

97
00:08:21,737 --> 00:08:24,437
How much money is in the leather pouch?

98
00:08:25,107 --> 00:08:27,527
Three Lumione and two-sevenths.

99
00:08:27,527 --> 00:08:31,947
That means you still owe forty-three and five-sevenths, right?

100
00:08:31,947 --> 00:08:34,367
I have a cunning plan.

101
00:08:34,827 --> 00:08:36,207
What is it?

102
00:08:36,207 --> 00:08:38,747
Don't get too excited. I don't know if it's any good.

103
00:08:41,047 --> 00:08:42,797
Are you serious?

104
00:08:42,797 --> 00:08:46,837
Yes. You'll be caught with certainty if you do it the usual way.

105
00:08:46,837 --> 00:08:50,717
But I have an idea of how to get away with it at little risk.

106
00:08:50,717 --> 00:08:53,017
R-Really?

107
00:09:05,987 --> 00:09:08,487
It's okay. I'm by your side.

108
00:09:10,657 --> 00:09:11,577
Yeah.

109
00:09:14,537 --> 00:09:17,277
I heard you wanted to discuss something important.

110
00:09:18,917 --> 00:09:21,287
Are you asking me to travel along that path?

111
00:09:21,287 --> 00:09:25,377
It <i>is</i> slightly dangerous, but you'll be fine.

112
00:09:25,377 --> 00:09:29,767
Has God not protected you up until now?

113
00:09:30,927 --> 00:09:31,807
Yes.

114
00:09:34,177 --> 00:09:38,897
But I've heard that mercenaries have been sighted around the area recently.

115
00:09:38,897 --> 00:09:42,227
God will protect you without fail.

116
00:09:42,227 --> 00:09:44,217
There's no need to worry.

117
00:09:44,937 --> 00:09:45,897
Okay.

118
00:09:45,897 --> 00:09:49,237
You're a wonderful shepherd.

119
00:09:49,237 --> 00:09:51,677
We're all very proud of you.

120
00:09:53,867 --> 00:09:56,357
Smuggling? Impossible!

121
00:09:56,357 --> 00:09:57,867
I wouldn't be so sure.

122
00:09:58,287 --> 00:10:00,747
You're out of your mind. Get out.

123
00:10:00,747 --> 00:10:05,727
I'm sure there have been many who tried this same plan in the past,

124
00:10:05,727 --> 00:10:07,587
only to be ultimately caught.

125
00:10:07,587 --> 00:10:09,747
If you know that, our talk should go quickly.

126
00:10:09,747 --> 00:10:15,467
People standing on the brink of ruin can't distinguish a reckless scheme from a perfect one.

127
00:10:15,467 --> 00:10:17,007
That's where you are right now!

128
00:10:17,467 --> 00:10:22,267
What if I tell you there's a skilled, trustworthy individual who can smuggle the gold?

129
00:10:24,947 --> 00:10:30,817
A person that skilled could make plenty of money without resorting to smuggling gold, right?

130
00:10:30,817 --> 00:10:32,527
It sounds too good to be true.

131
00:10:32,527 --> 00:10:37,157
What if I said that this person is talented but not making good money?

132
00:10:37,157 --> 00:10:38,827
Impossible.

133
00:10:38,827 --> 00:10:41,657
What kind of person could fit the description you've given?

134
00:10:41,947 --> 00:10:48,917
One who is skilled and employed in this town but is underpaid and in need of money.

135
00:10:49,547 --> 00:10:55,837
One who is unhappy because their employer leaves something to be desired.

136
00:10:57,767 --> 00:11:00,047
They're employed by the Church,

137
00:11:00,047 --> 00:11:04,557
and the Church says that smuggling gold is an act of treason.

138
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:07,427
There's no doubt they'll accept the job

139
00:11:07,427 --> 00:11:13,157
if it gives them an opportunity to frustrate the Church's ends while receiving compensation for their work.

140
00:11:13,157 --> 00:11:16,617
The odds of betrayal are also close to zero.

141
00:11:17,617 --> 00:11:21,457
I'm sure you'll be as convinced as I am when you hear the name of this person.

142
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:28,547
In that case, why don't you smuggle gold yourself?

143
00:11:28,547 --> 00:11:33,337
Why would you tell me about the idea when you know that your share will become smaller as a result?

144
00:11:33,337 --> 00:11:36,427
The payment deadline for my debt is today.

145
00:11:36,427 --> 00:11:39,807
I'll be incarcerated by the trading house at sunset.

146
00:11:39,807 --> 00:11:43,557
And I've managed to gather only this.

147
00:11:47,567 --> 00:11:49,437
Take it as collateral and put your trust in me.

148
00:11:50,237 --> 00:11:51,647
Here's what I want.

149
00:11:52,397 --> 00:11:55,017
I request that the repayment be deferred,

150
00:11:55,017 --> 00:11:59,417
and I also need you to invest your assets in the purchase of gold.

151
00:12:01,367 --> 00:12:02,577
Sir?

152
00:12:03,577 --> 00:12:06,037
Do you think you have the luxury of wavering?

153
00:12:06,037 --> 00:12:06,987
What's that?!

154
00:12:07,417 --> 00:12:08,417
Hey.

155
00:12:08,417 --> 00:12:11,617
One of your men just left.

156
00:12:12,997 --> 00:12:17,597
I have ears that are keen enough to unearth the deepest secrets.

157
00:12:17,597 --> 00:12:21,797
The men downstairs are planning to escape this sinking ship.

158
00:12:22,937 --> 00:12:25,017
See? Another one just left.

159
00:12:25,017 --> 00:12:29,017
At this rate, it's only a matter of days before this shop...

160
00:12:29,017 --> 00:12:30,317
Stop it!

161
00:12:32,107 --> 00:12:34,057
Mr. Lemerio, what do you think?

162
00:12:34,067 --> 00:12:38,907
You must know someone who can trade the smuggled gold.

163
00:12:38,907 --> 00:12:43,067
Will you help us execute this plan on relatively favorable terms to you?

164
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:45,697
Mr. Lemerio!

165
00:12:46,997 --> 00:12:48,497
Very well.

166
00:12:49,497 --> 00:12:50,617
Let's do it.

167
00:12:52,967 --> 00:12:55,207
May God forgive us.

168
00:13:01,717 --> 00:13:03,347
Call Liebert.

169
00:13:03,347 --> 00:13:04,137
Yes, sir.

170
00:13:10,567 --> 00:13:13,647
Looks like it's my turn.

171
00:13:13,647 --> 00:13:15,057
What do you mean by that?

172
00:13:16,027 --> 00:13:21,197
Do you think a good-natured man like you could pull one over on that girl?

173
00:13:21,197 --> 00:13:25,317
There are innocent people in this world who prefer good-natured men.

174
00:13:25,647 --> 00:13:28,827
You certainly talk a lot for someone who doesn't know anything about females.

175
00:13:29,247 --> 00:13:33,377
You just drove Lemerio into a corner for me.

176
00:13:36,967 --> 00:13:39,637
Let me deal with her on my own.

177
00:13:40,387 --> 00:13:44,927
I'm the one who ended up with worthless goods due to my own greed.

178
00:13:45,307 --> 00:13:49,017
If I have you convince her so I can avoid feeling guilty, that means I'm hopeless.

179
00:13:49,017 --> 00:13:54,557
Curses! And here I thought I'd be able to add to the list of favors I've done for you and cash them in later on.

180
00:13:54,567 --> 00:13:56,857
Phew! That was a close one.

181
00:14:04,907 --> 00:14:05,907
Hello!

182
00:14:07,617 --> 00:14:10,577
Mr. Lawrence and... Miss Holo?

183
00:14:11,457 --> 00:14:17,457
It must be the will of God for us to meet in front of the church.

184
00:14:18,797 --> 00:14:21,017
Even I'm not that easily fooled.

185
00:14:21,927 --> 00:14:26,087
Thank heavens. I've heard that lately there are those at services who have drunk too much of the Holy Blood.

186
00:14:26,597 --> 00:14:31,357
I can't drink much, so I only take a little bit of the wine.

187
00:14:31,937 --> 00:14:34,017
Do you have something you'd like to...

188
00:14:34,017 --> 00:14:37,527
Yes, I'd like to offer you a job.

189
00:14:37,527 --> 00:14:38,187
Really?

190
00:14:40,067 --> 00:14:41,187
I-I mean...

191
00:14:41,527 --> 00:14:45,327
Let's find a place to sit down and talk.

192
00:14:45,327 --> 00:14:46,237
Okay.

193
00:14:50,867 --> 00:14:52,487
Here's to our reunion!

194
00:15:00,087 --> 00:15:03,887
Miss Norah, you said you could travel as far as Lamtra, right?

195
00:15:03,887 --> 00:15:06,177
Y-Yes, I can.

196
00:15:06,177 --> 00:15:08,387
Can you even bring your flock along?

197
00:15:08,387 --> 00:15:09,887
If there aren't too many.

198
00:15:10,387 --> 00:15:13,897
I'd like to hire you for a slightly unusual job.

199
00:15:13,897 --> 00:15:15,677
You'll be paid twenty Lumione,

200
00:15:16,147 --> 00:15:18,737
and it won't be in the form of a banknote.

201
00:15:18,737 --> 00:15:19,987
I'll pay in cash.

202
00:15:20,447 --> 00:15:21,357
Whoa there.

203
00:15:22,237 --> 00:15:23,487
I'm sorry.

204
00:15:24,157 --> 00:15:27,617
D-Did you say twenty?

205
00:15:28,077 --> 00:15:29,697
Yes, twenty.

206
00:15:29,697 --> 00:15:33,377
It will be on contingency due to the risks involved, though.

207
00:15:33,377 --> 00:15:35,177
If you fail, you won't receive anything.

208
00:15:35,997 --> 00:15:36,657
Okay.

209
00:15:37,087 --> 00:15:44,217
Your job is to venture out with your sheep and return them safe and sound.

210
00:15:44,217 --> 00:15:47,297
You only need to do what you normally would as a shepherd.

211
00:15:47,807 --> 00:15:50,727
It must be a dangerous task

212
00:15:51,227 --> 00:15:53,007
if you're willing to pay twenty Lumione.

213
00:15:53,477 --> 00:15:54,977
I won't deny that.

214
00:15:55,397 --> 00:16:00,937
I won't force you to accept, and I'm willing to let you think it over.

215
00:16:02,657 --> 00:16:06,937
Guild membership fees are one Lumione at most, aren't they?

216
00:16:06,937 --> 00:16:12,367
With twenty, you'll be able to rent a house and take care of your daily expenses, working without worry.

217
00:16:13,017 --> 00:16:16,197
When the time comes, you'd even be able to obtain a business permit with ease.

218
00:16:16,197 --> 00:16:19,627
Then you'd be the mistress of Norah Dressmakers.

219
00:16:20,457 --> 00:16:25,307
Miss Norah, had you planned to join the tailor's guild in this city?

220
00:16:25,997 --> 00:16:29,387
No, I was thinking about another town.

221
00:16:29,387 --> 00:16:30,307
I see.

222
00:16:33,477 --> 00:16:36,727
But the sprawling size of this city is appealing, isn't it?

223
00:16:36,727 --> 00:16:40,527
It can be difficult to live in an unfamiliar town with no friends,

224
00:16:40,527 --> 00:16:45,307
but you probably want to get away from the Church in this city, right?

225
00:16:45,307 --> 00:16:47,867
T-That's not true.

226
00:16:47,867 --> 00:16:54,537
The harder you work to protect the sheep that the church entrusts you with,

227
00:16:54,537 --> 00:16:58,367
the more they suspect you of using pagan witchcraft.

228
00:16:58,917 --> 00:17:00,077
Am I wrong?

229
00:17:00,587 --> 00:17:08,577
They send you to places ordinary shepherds would never tread for the sake of revealing your true identity,

230
00:17:09,177 --> 00:17:13,597
by claiming that safer territories are occupied by other shepherds.

231
00:17:14,517 --> 00:17:21,017
I imagine that they intend to keep sending you to dangerous
places until you're attacked by wolves or mercenaries.

232
00:17:21,017 --> 00:17:25,647
They'll do this day after day until they find evidence of your heathen nature.

233
00:17:26,907 --> 00:17:29,697
I was a victim of a similar situation.

234
00:17:29,697 --> 00:17:31,187
Let me state it clearly.

235
00:17:31,827 --> 00:17:34,027
The Church of this town is lower than swine!

236
00:17:42,077 --> 00:17:44,007
This is why we came up with a plan.

237
00:17:44,667 --> 00:17:48,967
We'll cause a little trouble for the Church, make some money, and leave for another town.

238
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:50,217
What do you think?

239
00:17:50,217 --> 00:17:52,637
What do you plan to do?

240
00:17:54,307 --> 00:17:55,887
Smuggle gold.

241
00:17:57,137 --> 00:17:58,347
There's no way...

242
00:18:01,017 --> 00:18:03,937
How will I be involved in this?

243
00:18:04,777 --> 00:18:10,437
We'll hide the gold inside the stomachs of your sheep in order to pass the checkpoints of this town.

244
00:18:18,247 --> 00:18:21,447
Can you tell me the rest of plan?

245
00:18:22,037 --> 00:18:26,247
The price of gold is extremely high in every town under the influence of the Church.

246
00:18:26,247 --> 00:18:31,957
That's why the ideal place to get it is in the pagan town of Lamtra.

247
00:18:32,597 --> 00:18:37,597
All of the safe roads leading to Lamtra are crowded with people,

248
00:18:37,597 --> 00:18:42,057
and it has been the territory of other shepherds for ages.

249
00:18:43,187 --> 00:18:49,737
I'd be able to travel through desolate roads without being suspected of any wrongdoing,

250
00:18:49,737 --> 00:18:54,437
and that route is also the shortest distance between Lamtra and this town.

251
00:18:54,907 --> 00:18:56,537
That's right.

252
00:18:56,537 --> 00:19:01,017
You're being mistreated by the Church, aren't you?

253
00:19:01,747 --> 00:19:05,947
This plan serves as an ideal opportunity to take revenge against them.

254
00:19:06,327 --> 00:19:11,637
The Church's two biggest sources of income are tithes and the gold trade, after all.

255
00:19:13,847 --> 00:19:17,557
But if we're caught, the punishments will be heavy.

256
00:19:17,557 --> 00:19:21,557
And once the job is done, you'll have to leave this town to be safe.

257
00:19:21,557 --> 00:19:23,267
And so...

258
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:25,597
The reward is twenty Lumione.

259
00:19:41,897 --> 00:19:43,737
Please allow me to do it.

260
00:19:46,627 --> 00:19:48,377
It'll be my pleasure.

261
00:19:48,377 --> 00:19:49,917
Likewise.

262
00:19:50,297 --> 00:19:51,257
Um...

263
00:19:52,127 --> 00:19:53,427
What is it?

264
00:19:53,427 --> 00:19:58,377
I wouldn't have accepted if someone else had approached me with the idea.

265
00:19:58,747 --> 00:20:02,387
I decided to do it because it was you, Mr. Lawrence.

266
00:20:13,987 --> 00:20:16,457
Shouldn't you be happier about this?

267
00:20:16,457 --> 00:20:18,237
Everything went perfectly.

268
00:20:20,057 --> 00:20:25,527
I don't care how great the profit—nothing exists to balance out the wager of a person's life.

269
00:20:25,957 --> 00:20:27,417
Indeed.

270
00:20:27,417 --> 00:20:32,587
And just talking up the profit like that is little different from fraud.

271
00:20:33,677 --> 00:20:38,597
Merchants always say that if you get bamboozled into a bad contract, you're the fool at fault.

272
00:20:38,597 --> 00:20:40,717
But who's the person we're dealing with here?

273
00:20:40,717 --> 00:20:43,927
She's only a shepherd girl who doesn't know how the world works.

274
00:20:44,597 --> 00:20:47,967
It's true that the girl's smile looked innocent enough.

275
00:20:49,267 --> 00:20:53,187
Honestly, you're far too kind for your own good.

276
00:20:55,897 --> 00:21:01,217
That little girl is not a mere lamb who exists just to be hunted and eaten.

277
00:21:03,497 --> 00:21:09,457
She's a brave sheep who's decided to mingle with the predators.

278
00:21:09,457 --> 00:21:14,207
She might even be a different animal wearing sheep's skin.

279
00:21:15,047 --> 00:21:16,937
I don't want to admit it,

280
00:21:18,177 --> 00:21:20,547
but she's a shepherd that even I approve of.

281
00:21:21,217 --> 00:21:24,097
You're not in the wrong here,

282
00:21:24,097 --> 00:21:26,437
so try to put others before you a bit less often.

283
00:21:28,017 --> 00:21:33,437
In any case, I have to do everything I can so that we all end up laughing.

284
00:21:33,437 --> 00:21:35,067
Is that so?

285
00:21:35,067 --> 00:21:39,227
Would it not be better for just the two of us to have the last laugh?

286
00:21:40,527 --> 00:21:42,277
I wouldn't mind that either,

287
00:21:43,197 --> 00:21:46,617
but I'd prefer if we could all be happy.

288
00:21:46,617 --> 00:21:48,667
There you go again.

289
00:21:48,667 --> 00:21:49,877
Is that a problem?

290
00:21:49,877 --> 00:21:51,117
Not at all.

291
00:21:54,717 --> 00:21:58,427
Sir, are you really going to go through with this?

292
00:21:59,007 --> 00:22:00,887
I have to do it.

293
00:22:00,887 --> 00:22:02,427
I have to...

294
00:22:02,427 --> 00:22:05,927
I don't have a choice, Liebert!

295
00:23:40,847 --> 00:23:43,817
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Pack of Pups."</i>

296
00:23:45,957 --> 00:23:49,207
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and a Pack of Pups."</i>

